# Edge & embedded emphasis

Product mandate: **good inference at any scale**, with emphasis on **edge and
embedded** (WASM, Raspberry Pi–class ARM). Normative prose:
[`docs/mandate.md`](../../docs/mandate.md).

When adding features, loaders, backends, or acceptance:

- Prefer designs that work under **tight RAM/CPU** and explicit budgets
  ([US-025](../../docs/stories/025-bounded-model-admission.md)–[US-029](../../docs/stories/029-capability-aware-kernels.md)).
- Treat **embedded WASM** and **small-board live** paths as first-class, not demos bolted on after a GPU-only design.
- Server/GPU scale remains in scope when it shares the same loaders, telemetry, and DI wiring — do not fork a “cloud engine.”
- Park datacenter-only techniques in [`docs/inspiration/`](../../docs/inspiration/) until a user story claims them.
